From: kakwa <carpentier.pf@gmail.com>
Subject: Use packaged crates for the offline chroot build
The upstream tree pulls a number of dependencies straight from git
(pop-os/libcosmic, pop-os/winit, wash2/accesskit, pop-os/softbuffer,
pop-os/smithay-clipboard, pop-os/window_clipboard, pop-os/dbus-settings-bindings,
pop-os/cosmic-settings, pop-os/cosmic-settings-daemon, pop-os/cosmic-comp,
pop-os/cosmic-notifications, pop-os/cosmic-osk, pop-os/cosmic-panel,
pop-os/cosmic-protocols, iced-rs/cryoglyph, jackpot51/rust-atomicwrites).

An offline chroot build (cowbuilder/pbuilder with no network access) cannot
fetch any of these git repositories, and the Debian cargo wrapper additionally
replaces the crates.io registry with the Debian-provided one, so version
requirements that only match a git commit must be relaxed to the versions that
are actually packaged.

This patch:
 - removes the `[patch."https://github.com/smithay/client-toolkit.git"]`
   section: no crate in the workspace depends on that git URL, and the entry
   is otherwise rejected because the packaged smithay-client-toolkit is 0.19.2
   while the entry requires ^0.20.0;
 - switches the workspace and per-crate dependencies from git sources to the
   packaged crate versions;
 - relaxes version requirements to the versions available in the Debian
   archive.

The resolved dependency graph stays equivalent: every crate that was fetched
from a git repository has a packaged counterpart providing the same API, and
the versions chosen here match the packaged ones.

